/-!
# Serre's global generation theorem for ample line bundles

Let `X` be a scheme, `a` an ample line-bundle class on `X` (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple`), and `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type. Then there is a bound `n₀ : ℕ` such that for every
`n ≥ n₀` and every invertible sheaf `M` representing `aⁿ`, the twist `F ⊗ M` is generated by
finitely many global sections (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_generatingSections_tensor`). No
Noetherian or explicit quasi-separatedness hypothesis on `X` is needed, since a scheme carrying an
ample line bundle is automatically quasi-compact and quasi-separated.

The proof reduces to Serre's theorem for an invertible sheaf whose affine nonvanishing loci cover
`X` (`Scheme.Modules.eventually_exists_generatingSections_tensor_tensorPow`):

1. By quasi-compactness (`IsAmple.compactSpace`), `X` is covered by finitely many affine
   nonvanishing loci of global sections of positive powers `L^{dᵢ}`. Raising each section to the
   power `m / dᵢ` for `m = ∏ dᵢ` preserves its nonvanishing locus
   (`Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection`), producing finitely many global sections of
   a single positive power `Lᵐ` whose affine nonvanishing loci cover `X`
   (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_pow_iSup_nonvanishingLocus_eq_top`, Stacks Tag 01PR).
2. Applying `eventually_exists_generatingSections_tensor_tensorPow` to `Lᵐ` and each of the
   finitely many residue twists `F ⊗ Lʳ` (`0 ≤ r < m`) yields a uniform threshold `n₀` beyond
   which every twist `F ⊗ M` with `[M] = aⁿ` is generated by finitely many global sections
   (Hartshorne, Theorem II.5.17; Stacks Tag 01Q3).

As consequences:

* For any invertible sheaf `K`, the twists `K ⊗ M` are globally generated for `n ≥ n₀`
  (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct`).
* Tensoring a surjection `𝒪_X^k ↠ F ⊗ M` with an inverse `K` (`M ⊗ K ≅ 𝒪_X`) gives an epimorphism
  from a finite direct sum `K^⊕k ↠ F` (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_epi_biproduct`).

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01PR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PR) and
  [Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3).
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
